      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Circuit QED made the interaction of individual artificial atoms and microwave photons a controllable laboratory reality, opening a durable new regime of quantum optics.",
        "attribution": "Blais and Girvin supplied central theoretical formulations, while Schoelkopf established decisive experimental architecture; the broad community contribution remains substantial.",
        "maturity": "The methods are reproducible across laboratories and underpin a major branch of superconducting quantum science.",
        "uncertainties": [
