        "Mark Saffman",
        "Antoine Browaeys",
        "Mikhail D. Lukin"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Rydberg blockade converted strong atom-atom interactions into programmable quantum arrays, creating an exceptionally flexible quantum-optical many-body platform.",
        "attribution": "Saffman developed decisive blockade and gate concepts, while Browaeys and Lukin drove influential experimental array realizations.",
        "maturity": "Large programmable arrays and coherent control are now established in several laboratories.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The development is recent, and the precise boundary between foundational discovery and rapidly evolving technology is still settling."
        ]
      }
    },
